.TH START-DARPA-SPILLSERVER 1 "September 24, 2026" "darpa_spillserver 1.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
start-darpa-spillserver \- start the DARPA Spill Information Server in the background
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./start\-darpa\-spillserver.sh
.RB [ \-c | \-\-config
.IR FILE ]
.RI [ SERVER-OPTIONS ...]
.PP
.B .\e start\-darpa\-spillserver.ps1
.RB [ \-Config
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-Wait
.IR SECONDS ]
.RB [ \-\- ]
.RI [ SERVER-OPTIONS ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Starts
.BR darpa-spill-server (1)
from a checkout, detached from the terminal, for hosts where it is not run as a
service. A service install should use the systemd unit in
.I docs/DEPLOYMENT.md
instead. The shell script runs on Linux and macOS; the PowerShell script on
Windows 11.
.PP
Both scripts:
.IP 1. 4
Refuse to start a second copy: if the PID file names a live
.B darpa\-spill\-server
process they report it and exit 0. The process's command line is checked, not
just that the PID exists, so a stale PID file never matches an unrelated
process; a stale file is removed.
.IP 2. 4
Run
.B darpa\-spill\-server \-\-print\-config
with the same options, which contacts nothing, to reject a bad configuration
before starting and to find the address the health check should use (a
wildcard bind is checked on 127.0.0.1).
.IP 3. 4
Start the server in the background and write its PID file.
.IP 4. 4
Poll
.I /api/health
once a second with
.BR "darpa\-spill\-client \-k health" ,
and report success only once it answers, so that a port already in use or a
failure during startup is reported here. If the server exits while starting,
the tail of its log is shown.
.PP
On Linux and macOS the server is given its own session (via Python's
.BR os.setsid ,
since macOS has no
.BR setsid (1)),
so it survives logging out, and its standard output and error are appended to
one log, each start marked with a header line. On Windows it is a hidden
process whose output and errors go to
.I run\e spillserver.log
and
.IR run\e spillserver.err.log .
If
.I venv
does not exist, the PowerShell script runs
.B bootstrap.ps1 \-BuildCpp no
first; the shell script asks you to run
.B ./bootstrap.sh
instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR " (sh), " \-Config " " \fIFILE\fR " (ps1)"
Configuration file. Default: \fB$SPILL_CONFIG\fR, else
.I ./spillserver.yaml
if it exists, else
.IR config/spillserver.yaml .
.TP
.BI \-Wait " SECONDS"
(ps1) Seconds to wait for the health check. Default \fB$SPILL_WAIT\fR, else
\fB30\fR.
.TP
.I SERVER-OPTIONS
Anything else is passed to
.BR darpa-spill-server (1),
e.g.
.BR "\-\-port 8081" .
In PowerShell, put
.B \-\-
before them.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SPILL_CONFIG
Configuration file, when none is given on the command line.
.TP
.B SPILL_PIDFILE
PID file. Default
.IR run/spillserver.pid .
.TP
.B SPILL_LOGFILE
Output log. Default
.IR run/spillserver.log .
.TP
.B SPILL_WAIT
Seconds to wait for the health check. Default \fB30\fR.
.PP
The server itself also reads its
.B DARPA_SPILL_
variables and
.I .env
file; see
.BR darpa-spill-server (1).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I venv/
The virtual environment made by
.BR darpa-spillserver-bootstrap (1).
.TP
.I run/spillserver.pid
.TQ
.I run/spillserver.log
.TQ
.I run\e spillserver.err.log
PID file and logs.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The server is up and answering, or was already running.
.TP
.B 1
The server was not found, exited during startup, or did not answer within
the wait.
.TP
.B 2
The configuration was rejected; nothing was started.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.EX
\&./start\-darpa\-spillserver.sh
\&./start\-darpa\-spillserver.sh \-c config/spillserver\-near.yaml
\&./start\-darpa\-spillserver.sh \-\-port 8081
SPILL_WAIT=60 ./start\-darpa\-spillserver.sh
.EE
.RE
.PP
On Windows:
.PP
.RS
.EX
powershell \-ExecutionPolicy Bypass \-File .\e start\-darpa\-spillserver.ps1
\&.\e start\-darpa\-spillserver.ps1 \-Config config\e spillserver\-near.yaml \-\- \-\-port 8081
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR stop-darpa-spillserver (1),
.BR darpa-spillserver-bootstrap (1),
.BR darpa-spill-server (1),
.BR darpa-spill-client (1)
.SH REPORTING BUGS
Report defects at
\fBhttps://github.com/NovaDAQ/DARPA\-SpillServer/issues\fR.
